From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Taixin Reverse <reverse@taixin.local>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 16:03:30 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] router: probe before writing the ipv6 forwarding knob

'echo 0 > /proc/sys/net/ipv6/... 2>/dev/null || true' still prints
ash's 'can't create ...: nonexistent directory' when the kernel has
no ipv6 stack: the redirection fails before stderr is duped, so the
suppression never applies. Test for the knob instead.
---
 .../board/cvitek/SG200X/overlay/etc/init.d/S60routing     | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/buildroot/board/cvitek/SG200X/overlay/etc/init.d/S60routing b/buildroot/board/cvitek/SG200X/overlay/etc/init.d/S60routing
index 654c81b94..64f47ba1b 100755
--- a/buildroot/board/cvitek/SG200X/overlay/etc/init.d/S60routing
+++ b/buildroot/board/cvitek/SG200X/overlay/etc/init.d/S60routing
@@ -105,7 +105,13 @@ start() {
 	echo 0 > /proc/sys/net/ipv4/conf/all/rp_filter
 	echo 0 > /proc/sys/net/ipv4/conf/default/rp_filter
 	echo 0 > /proc/sys/net/ipv4/conf/all/accept_redirects
-	echo 0 > /proc/sys/net/ipv6/conf/all/forwarding 2>/dev/null || true
+	# The ipv6 stack may be absent from the kernel entirely. ash prints
+	# "can't create ...: nonexistent directory" for a failed redirection
+	# even with 2>/dev/null (the redirection is attempted before stderr
+	# is duped), so probe for the knob instead of relying on stderr.
+	if [ -e /proc/sys/net/ipv6/conf/all/forwarding ]; then
+		echo 0 > /proc/sys/net/ipv6/conf/all/forwarding
+	fi
 	# route_localnet on the WAN iface: lets a port forward whose target is a
 	# loopback address (127.0.0.0/8 — e.g. a service that binds only to
 	# 127.0.0.1) actually be delivered. Without it, a packet DNAT'd to 127.x
